{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-08T07:02:11.817Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"7b9ffc55379beb42a217be16","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-08T07:02:11.817Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Review round two fixes for the kernel and guard threads: deterministic covers and domains are now served through bounded content-keyed reuse (a fresh twelve-binary-factor cover still measures about one second, while equal-content recomputation and every later packet page add zero fresh computations), the submitted-text guard rejects only absolute home paths at path-token starts so public URLs and relative paths pass, and guardSubmitted enforces an aggregate 200000-visit traversal budget that counts shared-subtree revisits. Reuse returns isolated copies, stays keyed by exact model content so a changed model recomputes, and readState still refuses tampered stored plans. Regression tests: covers-and-domains reuse across equal models and packet pages, a public-path must-allow corpus, and a shared-subtree DAG refusal. Behavioral revert proof: with reuse bypassed, the budget removed and the path pattern rolled back, each focused test fails red with AssertionError and all eight restored variants pass green."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-08T07:02:11.817Z"}],"before_hash":"51af2ffc863563fd4f452deedc47b8dbc3dd794b8bba20c3fdd8319b8d2e7787","after_hash":"8545aa2ce7ef635919a04b663020cfdae9e11d43ba2591d678c47756de827e57","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"d02b59b690b24189b860d8ef7b90bc14a6fee3f062d7fe5fa5f53c87c106040f"}
